DS3D RealSense data loader is an implementation of `ds3d::dataloader` which
captures aligned depth and colour frames from an Intel RealSense camera and
produces a `ds3d::datamap` for each capture, together with the camera intrinsic
and depth-scale parameters needed by the depth-to-point-cloud filter.

DS3D is framework agnostic. There is no gstreamer/Glib dependencies. Any framework could
simply wrap DS3D modules.

`libnvds_3d_dataloader_realsense.so` is built from these source files. and the
RealSense data loader is created through API `createRealsenseDataloader`.
Application users can call this API to instantiate a RealSense dataloader.

In compatible with Gstreamer plugins, `ds3d::dataloader` could be loaded into GstAppSrc
in runtime through API `NvDs3D_CreateDataLoaderSrc(config)`
The config content shall as:

    type: ds3d::dataloader
    out_caps: ds3d/datamap
    custom_lib_path: libnvds_3d_dataloader_realsense.so
    custom_create_function: createRealsenseDataloader
    config_body:
       ...

Any custom `ds3d::dataloader` must derive from `ds3d::SyncImplDataLoader` for sychronized
dataloader. And implement the following interfaces:

    ErrCode startImpl(const std::string& content, const std::string& path) override;
    ErrCode readDataImpl(GuardDataMap& datamap) override;
    ErrCode stopImpl() override;
    ErrCode flushImpl() override;

In addition, users also need export a C-API for application to intiate this dataloader.
The exported C-API name is not limited. In this sample, it is `createRealsenseDataloader`.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime
- Intel RealSense SDK (librealsense2) on the target at run time. It is not
  needed at build time: the library links against the stub built by
  `ds3d/stub/realsense`, and the headers are vendored under
  `ds3d/3rdparty/realsense2`. To capture from a real camera, install the SDK per
  https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/distribution_linux.md

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this `ds3d::dataloader` lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
  The RealSense link stub is built automatically if it is missing.
- Verify `libnvds_3d_dataloader_realsense.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
